"Yoto App updates (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/yoto-app-updates-BJZeKFsQGg)\nciteturn818search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week;   * Setup: new setup images to better guide how to generate a setup code ... from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (turn off the alarm by pressing any button on the player)\n\n## Yoto App updates\n\nJuly 20 2026 9:39am • Est. Read Time: 21 MIN\n\n#### See the features for the latest update we have made to the Yoto app, as well as all the previous updates.\n\nTip: you can check which version of the Yoto app you have by going to the Menu tab (in the app) where it is listed at  the bottom of the screen. \n\nYoto app updates\n\nWe release updates for the app regularly, bringing in new features, optimising performance and squishing bugs that come along from time to time. It's probably a good idea to switch on auto updates for the app, if you don't have this already.\n\nYoto app (Beta)\n\nWe make an app beta available for external testing before we promote the new release to the app stores. Whilst we test extensively and endeavour to ensure the app operates in beta without issues, there are times when glitches may arise. Participating in the app beta gives you access to new features ahead of time but with the caveat that there may be glitches that we haven't spotted. If you let us know at hello@yotoplay.com we can quickly put it right. To participate in the Yoto app beta, you can sign up via one of these links:\n\niPhone: https://testflight.apple.com/join/di4bwD5z\n\nAndroid: https://play.google.com/apps/testing/com.yotoplay.yoto\n\nLatest beta version\n\nYoto App v3.35 (22 Apr 2026)\n\n  * We've been busy behind the scenes – tidying, tweaking and giving the app a proper spruce-up. Tidier and easier to get around. Same Yoto magic, just with a little extra shine!\n\nLatest app version\n\nYoto App v3.34 (14 Apr 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nPrevious app versions\n\nYoto App v3.33 (1 Apr 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n  * Minimum supported OS is now iOS 17 and Android 10\n\nYoto App v3.32.1 (12 Mar 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.32 (11 Mar 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.31 (2 Mar 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.30 (9 Feb 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.29 (19 Jan 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.28.1 (5 Jan 2026)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.28 (5 Dec 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.27 (14 Nov 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.26 (29 Oct 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.25 (7 Oct 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.24 (4 Sep 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.23 (20 Aug 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.22 (5 Aug 2025)\n\n  * You can now add new members to your family from your app. Generate an invite code and send it to a parent or grandparent to your Yoto family.\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.21 (23 July 2025)\n\n    •    We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.20 (10 July 2025)\n\n    •    We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.19 (12 Jun 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.18 (2 Jun 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.17 (13 Mar 2025)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.16 (7 Apr 2025)\n\n  * Improvements to new minimised player and making it available on more screens\n  * Yoto Daily in the app from midnight of the daily episode\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.6\n\nUpdated navigation:\n\n  * The Menu & Player tabs have been merged into one new tab Settings\n  * To make it easier to create your own content we've moved My recordings, Make a playlist and Yoto Creators to a new tab, Create\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.5\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v3.4\n\nHelping to discover Club Collection content for you & your family!\n\nClub Collection:\n\n  * Filtering to the Club Collection for easier content discovery\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience.\n\nYoto App v3.3\n\nWe're excited to bring you the first additional update to Groups!\n\nGroups:\n\n  * Remove cards from a Group to keep everything up-to-date.\n  * Fix typos or change the name of your Group.\n  * Rotate the Group's randomised image to one of your choice.\n  * We've squashed some bugs and improved performance for a better app experience.\n\nYoto App v3.1/3.2\n\n  * Introducing Groups: You can now create Groups within your Family Library!\n  * Add any cards from your Family Library to a Group. Combine podcasts, radio streams, MYOs, free, and purchased cards into a Group. Add one card to multiple Groups. Create up to 20 Groups. Filter and search your card list to find cards to add to your Groups. Watch out for more updates to follow!\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience.\n\n\nYoto App v2.70 (12th Feb 2024)\n\n  * Yoto is now compatible with CarPlay / Android Auto! Access your favourite cards directly from your car's dashboard\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v2.69 (6th Feb 2024)\n\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v2.68 (28th Nov 2023)\n\n  * Referrals: Do you know a family who will love Yoto as much as yours? You can now find and share your referral code from the app to share with friends and earn points for yourself.\n  * Player Settings: If we notice an issue with your player, we will highlight this in your player settings. We will help you contact our Customer Happiness team to resolve any issues as quickly as possible.\n  * Player Setup: We’ve made the steps for setting up Wi-Fi and family account setup clearer.\n  * Update on iOS Compatibility: To enhance your experience, we’re now focusing on newer versions and will no longer support iOS 14.\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience.\n\nYoto App v2.67 (8th Nov 2023)\n\n  * Player setup: We've updated the player setup to provide you with essential information on safe usage\n  * Player setup: Our app now checks you are connected to the player before sending wifi credentials (iOS only)\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v2.66 (30th Oct 2023)\n\n  * Player Settings : Improved the player downloads screen for a clearer view of downloaded content and download tips\n  * Player Setup : Now, when pairing with an already paired player, the email address is partially hidden for your privacy\n  * We've made more space in the bottom navigation for an easier and smoother navigation experience (iOS only)\n  * MYO : You can now upload an MP3 from another app using your sharing screen (Android only)\n  * Fix for Android 14 issue where audio stops playing in the background\n  * We've squashed some bugs and made performance improvements for a better app experience\n\nYoto App v2.65 (10th Oct 2023)\n\n  * Club in the app: for UK, US & CA club subscribers, there's a new section with additional free content\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.64 (4th Oct 2023)\n\n  * Player setup: We’ve made improvements to the player setup flow.\n  * Player Settings: We’ve refreshed the look and feel of the night mode section of player settings.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.63 (14th Sept 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Upload and edit custom icons for your MYO tracks.\n  * Player Settings: We’ve refreshed the look of your player setting including dark mode support.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nAndroid only\n\n  * Fixed crash affecting large file uploads.\n\nYoto App v2.62 (4th Sept 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Take a photo or upload an image to personalize your MYO playlists\n  * Alarms: Enable and disable individual alarms with the flick of a switch\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload your own custom pixel artwork to tracks MYO track\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.61 (14th Aug 2023)\n\n  * MYO: You can now upload any MP3s from your phone to a MYO playlist from within the app.\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload any artwork to your MYO playlist without going to the MYO webpage.\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.60 (7th Aug 2023)\n\n  * MYO: Edit your MYO playlists in the app. Edit your playlist name and description. Rename, reorder and change the icons of your tracks.\n  * Coming soon in a future release: Upload any audio and artwork to your MYO playlist without going to the MYO webpage.\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nYoto App v2.59 (27th June 2023)\n\n  * Setup: new setup images to better guide how to generate a setup code\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.55 (12th May 2023)\n\n  * My recordings: an updated voice recordings screen in preparation for in-app upload to a playlist. Also now available in dark mode\n  * My recordings list: a refreshed list of recordings and removed friction with an optional file renaming\n  * My recordings voice recorder: a chime button to play a sound to help you to separate chapters\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.54 (21st Apr 2023)\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.53 (11th Apr 2023)\n\n  * Login: new in-app login and signup screens\n  * Maxi player: Apple AirPlay so that you can stream to other devices around your home (iOS only)\n  * Setup: improvements to the setup screens and a prominent MAC address to help you to connect to other networks\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.52 (2nd Mar 2023)\n\n  * Maxi player: card looping when playing on a player\n  * Maxi player: displaying the track icon of the currently playing track\n  * Minimised player: displaying the track icon of the currently playing track\n  * News & Players: a light restyle\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n  * Android 13 lock screen widget fix\n\nYoto App v2.51 (13th Feb 2023)\n\n  * Player downloads: a new section to display the current card queued for download\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.50 (2nd Feb 2023)\n\n  * Maxi player: card looping when playing on the phone. Player looping is coming soon!\n\n  * Maxi player: for streaming content a new animation indicates something is playing when the seek bar can't be displayed\n\n  * Pairing: a warning and confirmation when leaving an existing family to join another\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.49 (18th Jan 2023)\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.48 (16th Jan 2023)\n\n  * Bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.47 (12th Dec 2022)\n\n  * Menu: a troubleshooting test to ensure your network can get through to the Yoto cloud\n\n  * Store tab: added a club link to take you to the club page on the website\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.46 (1st Dec 2022)\n\n  * ALARMS!! from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (turn off the alarm by pressing any button on the player)\n  * Menu tab:switch between modes from the app menu\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.45 (22nd Nov 2022)\n\n  * ALARMS!! from player settings set up to 10 alarms to sound on your player (your player must be on beta).\n  * Player settings: player downloads view improvements\n  * Maxi player: time remaining added to the track position scrubber\n  * Maxi player: 'Scan a card' moved into the three dots menu\n  * Menu tab: light restyle\n  * Store tab: dark mode\n  * Voice recording permissions fix for Android 13\n  * Fix for missing right hand button section for Android 6 and 7\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.44 (14th Oct 2022)\n\n  * Maxi Player: pause & resume controls so you can pause a card for a moment without then having to find it in the library again\n  * Maxi Player: added more support for dark mode in the app\n  * Card details: volume control and a player picker\n  * Library: new empty state designs\n  * Players: new logged out and empty state designs\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.43 (16th Sept 2022)\n\nYoto App v2.38 (27th Apr 2022)\n\n  * Dropped support for iOS 12\n  * Maxi player: see the current position of the track playing and scrub forwards and backwards using the seekbar. In addition bump forwards/backwards buttons 15 seconds on the currently playing track\n  * Maxi player: set a custom sleep timer\n  * Library: search by author as well as title when viewing your cards\n  * Player settings Yoto Beta Labs: you can join the player beta from the app and if you're participating in it you can try out some of our experimental settings we're trialling with the players\n  * Shared cards: improvements for consuming shared cards\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.37 (4th Apr 2022)\n\n  * Library: we’ve added a ‘Scan a card’ button to make it more obvious you can scan a card to add it to your library\n  * Library: we've updated the Menu style to bring it up to date with the recent My Library design updates\n  * MYO: this now has a gallery view, like ‘My Cards’. In addition, you can now create custom artwork, reorder tracks and rename tracks. \nYoto App v2.34 (12th Dec 2021)\n\n  * Sleep timer: set a timer to stop your Player or Mini playing after a set period of minutes\n  * Remove a Library card: hide purchases from the app and then add them back in by playing them again\n  * Player MAC address: find your Player MAC address in Player settings\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.33 (24th Nov 2021)\n\n  * Player and app: visibility of what your Player or Mini is doing, its current and maximum volume, and what is playing on it\n  * App expanded player screen: a refreshed design with space for some upcoming features\n  * Track listings screen: a refreshed design and the ability to start individual tracks playing on your Player or Mini from the app\n  * Yoto Mini: setup screens for our new portable player\n  * Lots of bug fixes and performance improvements behind the scenes\n\nYoto App v2.32 (5th Oct 2021)\n\n  * Numerous bug fixes and performance improvements\n\nYoto App v2.31 (2nd Sept 2021)\n\n  * Player Settings: we have refreshed the Advanced section to follow the updates to the Day and Night mode sections in the last release\nYoto App v2.28 (30th June 2021)\n\n  * Splash: we’ve given the splash screen a makeover\n  * Discover: the Featured Audio tab has become Discover\n  * Navigation: we’ve made navigation of the library more intuitive and clearer you can swipe between content screens\n  * New users: we’ve given the app a refresh for new users to better explain what you can do in the app\n  * Setup: you can now connect the Player to your phone’s hotspot using one phone, not two!\n  * iPad: we’ve made the iPad screens full screen for a better tablet experience\n\nYoto App v2.27 (18th May 2021)\n\n  * Simplified join family/claim player pairing flow and screens\n  * Fixed voice recording for Android 11 users\n  * Fixed My Library blank screen bug affecting some iPhone users\n\nYoto App v2.26 (6th May 2021)\n\n  * Setup Improvements: including adding more specific details to our troubleshooting screens to make them more likely to solve real world setup issues. These updates are based on ongoing research and development we do in order to continually improve the setup process for Yoto Player.\n  * Plus: a bug fix for playing audio through other Bluetooth speakers (iPhone only), as well as some other general improvements to make things run smoothly.\n\nYoto App v2.17 (11th November 2020)\n\n  * Audio Record: Now you can record your own audio directly in the app, to make playlists you can link to cards to play on Yoto Player! No need to mess around with a 3rd party voice memo app, it all now happens in the Yoto app.\nGrandparents can make recordings which you can link to cards remotely for the kids. They just need to download the app, follow the “Set up a Yoto Player” steps (getting you to press the buttons and tell them the code over the phone if they can’t be there in person), and join your Family Account.\nAll playlists they make will now be visible in your app.\n\nYoto App v2.16 (23rd October 2020)\n\n  * Sleep Sounds: an exciting new feature coming to Yoto, Sleep Sounds is an addition to the My Library section of the app, and contains a selection of sounds to help sooth the restless when it’s time for bed. From White Noise, to Thundery Rain, to the gentle sound of a Devon Hedgerow. You can play these tracks from the app directly on your phone, or remotely through Yoto Player, or you can link them to a Make Your Own card in the normal way.\n  * Yoto Sleep Radio: within the Sleep Sounds area of the app, we have introduced a new radio station playing a selection of tracks for a calm and soothing bedtime. You can play this station from the app directly on your phone, or remotely through Yoto Player, or you can link it to a Make Your Own card in the normal way.\n  * Other fixes and improvements: layout tweaks for phones of different sizes, and more guidance on setting up Yoto Player to your Wi-Fi network when you have a network name (SSID) longer than 31 characters.\n\n  * Improved Player Setup options: you can now start this process from the device picker if you have not yet set up a Yoto Player. We made this change to give better options for people new to the app to do the thing they are likely to need to do first.\n\n Yoto App v2.10 (6th July 2020)\n\n  * Track/Chapter Listings: see tracks and play from a specific track when your phone is selected as the play-on device (when Yoto Player is selected you can see tracks and play the content from the beginning). Navigate to tracks/chapters by tapping a card image or title in My Library or tapping the “Chapters” link on the maxi player.\n  * New side bar navigation: on My Library for navigating between your library of content. This improves the navigation and paves the way for some exciting updates we have planned for the coming weeks.\n  * How To Guides: available from updated Menu screen\n  * Security update: see unverified members of your family account\n  * Family Account organisation improved: Remove a family member from the family account (only when you are verified). Helpful if things got mixed up during setup.\n\nYoto App v2.9 (10th June 2020)\n\n  * Updated tab bar navigation including News Feed section\n  * Updated device picker with position change for UX improvement\n  * Updated Yoto player\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4th Generation Yoto player FAQs (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/4th-generation-yoto-player-faqs-Byw2rlFzx)\nciteturn818search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; Grown-ups can customise both playlists in the Yoto App, adding audio from their library including stories, music, podcasts, radio stations, soundscapes, timers, sleep sounds and even your own recordings. ... On previous generations of Yoto Player, a single press of the right-hand button provides this quick-access function.\n\n## 4th Generation Yoto player FAQs\n\n## Do Yoto Cards work with all Yoto players?\n\nAlmost all Yoto Cards work with Yoto Player 4th Gen and Yoto Mini 4th Gen. The first time you play a card, make sure your player is connected to Wi-Fi so the audio can be downloaded.\n\nInteractive card compatibility coming soon. Our 4th Gen Yoto players run on an all-new platform, so a few features aren’t available just yet. This is temporary, and we’re working to make them available as soon as possible. We’ll keep this page updated with the latest information.\n\n## What is the difference between Yoto Player and Yoto Mini?\n\nYoto Player 4th Gen is made for family life at home, while Yoto Mini 4th Gen is designed to take Yoto on the go.\n\nYoto Player 4th Gen is the heart of the family home, with features to help with sleep, mornings and evening routines. Its full-panel night light creates a soothing glow, while the stereo sound is great for music, getting immersed in a story or settling down with sleep sounds.\n\nYoto Mini 4th Gen is the smaller, portable option, perfect for travel and adventures. It shares many of the same great Yoto features as Player, including the new Green Button, giving kids quick access to personal playlists of up to 20 titles for day and night, even when their Yoto Cards aren't to hand. Instead of the Yoto Player's full-panel night light, Mini prioritises portability and durability, with an IP67 water and dust-resistant design that's ready for the rough and tumble of childhood.\n\n## How does the Green Button work?\n\nThe Green Button gives kids quick access to their favourite audio, no Yoto Card needed. Just twist to browse and press to play.\n\nThere are two playlists: one for daytime and one for night time, each holding up to 20 titles. Yoto Daily and Yoto Radio are included in the daytime playlist by default, with Yoto Sleep Radio ready for night time.\n\nGrown-ups can customise both playlists in the Yoto App, adding audio from their library including stories, music, podcasts, radio stations, soundscapes, timers, sleep sounds and even your own recordings.\n\nOnce added, compatible audio downloads to the player, so kids can browse and listen even when they’re offline or on the move. Some audio, including radio stations and podcasts, requires an internet connection to stream.\n\nUsing the Green Button is simple:\n\n  * Twist to browse through titles and see their artwork on the display.\n\n  * Press to play the title you’ve chosen.\n\n  * Press again to pause.\n\n  * Press and hold to eject the audio and return to the clock.\n\n  * Press when no audio is playing to instantly play the first title in the current day or night playlist. By default, that’s Yoto Daily during the day and Yoto Sleep Radio at night.\n\nGrown-ups can change which title appears first in either playlist at any time in the Yoto App.\n\nOn previous generations of Yoto Player, a single press of the right-hand button provides this quick-access function.\n\n## What is the difference between the old and new Yoto players?\n\nYoto Player and Yoto Mini 4th Gen offer kids more choice, are more personal and are better equipped for family life.\n\n  * More choice for kids: The new Green Button and Day & Night Modes give kids even more independence over their listening, letting them twist straight to their favourites – handy when their favourite Yoto Card “must be here somewhere”.\n\n  * Made for family routines: Day & Night Modes make it easy to have different favourites ready for different parts of the day – from Yoto Daily over breakfast to sleep sounds at bedtime. There are handy features like toothbrush timers too, while Yoto Player's new full-panel night light gives families even more ways to set the mood for bedtime, wake-up and everything in between. And Yoto Mini is ready to come along for it all, with IP67 water and dust resistance for the rough and tumble of childhood.\n\n  * A big upgrade on the inside, too: We've overhauled the technology inside both players, informed by feedback from our community of Yoto families. Audio downloads to the player faster, interactions feel more responsive, and improved Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity make connecting to the Yoto App and Bluetooth headphones smoother and more reliable.\n\nAnd there's more to come. The new technology inside 4th Gen gives us greater scope to develop the Yoto experience over time, bringing new features and enhancements to Yoto Player and Yoto Mini.\n\n## What is the display for?\n\nThe display brings a visual dimension to Yoto's audio-first experience. Title artwork helps kids browse and choose what they want to listen to using the Green Button - much like picking a Yoto Card from their card case - while pixel icons help them navigate chapters and tracks as they listen.\n\nWhen audio isn't playing, the display also works as a clock, with customisable day and night settings that can help with family routines - including acting as an okay-to-wake cue.\n\n## What else do I get when I buy a Yoto player?\n\nThere's plenty to get you started! Every Yoto Player and Yoto Mini comes with a USB-C charging cable and a Welcome Card, which doubles as your first Make Your Own Card. You'll also find a set of fun stickers so kids can personalise their Card and make it their own. Grown-ups can then add their own recordings or audio from their library or the Yoto App, ready to pop in and play.\n\nYou'll also find a digital Yoto Card ready to go in your Yoto App library – Journey Jams with Yoto Mini and 5 Minute Stories From Around The World with Yoto Player. It's a great first listen, and an easy way to try adding audio to the Green Button or your new Make Your Own Card.\n\nAnd there's plenty more to discover in the Yoto App. Alongside managing your players and Yoto Card library, you'll find award-winning podcasts, multiple radio stations from Yoto and our partners, monthly digital Yoto Cards, sleep sounds and soundscapes, alarms and handy timers for everything from brushing teeth to homework.\n\nThe App is also home to Create, where grown-ups can record or add their own audio, ready to use with a Make Your Own Card or add to a Green Button playlist. It's a mix of free audio to discover and useful features to help with everyday family routines.\n\n## What are the benefits of audio on a Yoto player?\n\nAudio on Yoto gives kids the freedom to choose what they want to listen to and enjoy it their way – whether they're getting lost in a story, dancing to music, learning something new or listening together with family and friends. It's listening that puts kids in control.\n\nFor grown-ups, Yoto offers confidence in what kids are exploring. The Yoto catalogue is carefully curated with young listeners in mind, with stories, music, podcasts and more ready to discover. Grown-ups can then shape the experience around their family, from choosing new Yoto Cards to personalising Green Button playlists and adding their own audio.\n\nAnd there's plenty worth discovering. Kids can enjoy much-loved characters and stories including The Gruffalo, Winnie-the-Pooh and Harry Potter, explore our collection of Yoto Originals, or tune in to free audio like the award-winning Yoto Daily podcast.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsing the Yoto App on iOS and Android (https://support.yotoplay.com/en_gb/using-the-yoto-app-on-ios-and-android-ryJtFi7Me)\nciteturn818search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last week;   * Access how to Make Your Own guides to help you to create your own content ... Set-up up to 10 alarms.\n\n## Using the Yoto App on iOS and Android\n\nJuly 17 2026 2:50pm • Est. Read Time: 4 MIN\n\n#### Getting started with the Yoto app\n\nIf you are a brand-new user, choose Set up your player from either the landing screen or the Settings section.\n\nAs a second parent or family member with a player that has already been set up, choose Join a Family Account (from either the landing screen or the Settings section of the app).\n\nNews tab\n\nImage: Yoto App - News tabThis is where you can see up-to-date news from Yoto, tips on how to use your player and articles on things we find interesting, and hopefully you may too.\n\nCreate tab\n\nImage\n\nThis is the hub of Create in the app. Here you'll be able to:\n\n  * Record yourself narrating a story\n  * Access your previous recordings\n  * Make a playlist with your recordings or from mp3s\n  * Discover content from other creators on our community site: https://yoto.space\n  * Access how to Make Your Own guides to help you to create your own content\n\nLibrary tab\n\nThe library is the heart of the app. \n\nImage\n\nFrom here, you can:\n\n  * See (and play) all the cards you own\n  * See (and play) all Make Your Own playlists that you have created or that have been shared with you\n  * See (and play) all free cards (radio, podcasts, sleep etc.) you've added to your library\n  * See (and play) all Club Collection cards you've added to your library\n  * See and remotely control what's playing on a player\n\nTo play any of the content in the app, click the play icon, located on the image of that audio, and it will automatically play on the player or phone selected.\n\nThe Device Picker (above the main tab navigation and now playing info) allows you to select which device you are controlling, and playing audio on. \n\nThe Now Playing area shows you which piece of content you are playing on your phone, and allows you to pause or resume playing. Tapping on the Now Playing area opens up the Maxi Player. From here you can skip chapters or tracks and adjust the volume. \n\nFrom the Maxi Player, you can also: \n\n  * Set a sleep timer by tapping on the moon and stars icon in the right-hand corner.\n  * Choose the playback speed, rewind/ forward within the chapter by 15 seconds or by using the slider at the top.\n  * See the chapters of a card by pressing on the burger menu..\n\nDiscover tab\n\nImage: Yoto App - Discover tab\n\nThis is where you'll find and discover all of our free content covering radio, podcasts, sleep and stories. You can play all content from here and if you like it, you can add it to your own library for fast access. Just tap on the content to see the content details and tap 'Add to library'.\n\nSettings tab\n\nImage: Yoto App - Settings tabThis is where you can see details of who is in your Family Account and all of your players.\n\nYour registered details are at the top of the screen (this is the email address you used to sign in to the app). You will also be able to see details of all users (including you) in your Family Account who are paired with your players.\n\nUnder the list of users, you will also see all the players linked to your Family Account. \n\nEach listed player has a chevron icon. Tap this icon to manage settings for that player. \n\nSTATUS\n\nPlayer name - Personalize your player by giving it a name\n\nBattery level - view battery level of your player\n\nManage Wi-Fi - disconnect your player from the Wi-Fi or add a new network\n\nAudio Download Status - This shows you if all your cards have been downloaded to your player, or if some content still needs to download. If content is not downloaded fully, it will need to stream, which may cause playback issues if you have poor Wi-Fi in the location of your player\n\nALARMS\n\nSet-up up to 10 alarms. \n\nDAY AND NIGHT MODE\n\nMorning - Set a start time for day mode (the clock will change from moon to sun)\n\nBedtime - Set a start time for night mode (your clock will change from sun to moon)\n\nMorning Light / Nightlight Color (V2/V3 only) - Choose the color of the light on the rear of the Player. You can set different colors for night and day, so your child knows when it’s time to get up, even if the player is on its front. Only for Yoto Player: the Yoto Mini does not have a night light.\n\nAuto Display Brightness (V3 only) - Enable the Display Brightness to be auto-adjusted based on ambient light.\n\nDisplay Brightness - Set the default screen brightness during day/night modes when Auto Display Brightness is disabled/unavailable.\n\nVolume Limit - Set a limit for how loud your player will go for the day/night modes.\n\nNote: this volume limit applies to the Speaker and Wired Headphone outputs. The Yoto Wireless Headphones feature their own kid-safe volume limiting.\n\nRight Button Shortcuts - By default, your player will play Yoto Daily and Yoto Radio on first and second press during the day; and Yoto Sleep Radio on first press during the night. These can be edited to include French Language items and Timers. \n\nADVANCED\n\nBattery saver - Set how quickly the player display dims when no buttons or cards are touched, and when not on the dock. \n\nAuto Power-Off - Set how quickly the player switched off when no buttons or cards are touched while off charge. \n\nBluetooth pairing - Toggle this on to allow your player to enter Bluetooth mode, so you can play audio through your player just like any other Bluetooth speaker.\n\nBe aware, toggling this one does not turn on Bluetooth mode, it unlocks the feature, so you can subsequently enter Bluetooth mode by pressing the left-hand orange button for 3 seconds. \n\nHeadphone volume limit - set up a volume limit when audio is played with headphone.\n\n24-hour clock - Choose between a 12 and 24-hour clock for the front display of your player.\n\nAutomatic time zone - Ensure the time zone for your clock is set correctly (includes updates for daylight saving).\n\nYoto OS version - See which software version your player is on.\n\nYoto App version - See which software version your app is on.\n\nRegistration code - The six-letter code you used to set up your player. It is used to troubleshoot issues, if you have them.\n\nPlayer MAC Address \n\nYoto Beta labs - to join our beta user.\n\nUnpair this player from Family Account - to unpair a player from your account. "
